<title>USA: Contract for Alcoa workers extended.</title>
<headline>Contract for Alcoa workers extended.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aluminum Co of America and the United Autoworkers union have extended a contract covering workers at a Cleveland forging plant, after negotiations this week failed to produce a new agreement, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The current pact, originally set to expire last Tuesday at midnight (EST), was extended until midnight on September 4. Negotiations are ongoing, spokeswoman Joyce Saltzman said.</p>
<p>The contract covers 1,100 autoworkers at the plant, which makes forged aluminum parts for several industries including the auto industry.</p>
<p>Pittsburgh newsroom -- 412-471-7088</p>
</text>
